{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/568343-cruac-rites-rain-lvl3-coils-of-apep-lvl4","id":568343,"title":"Cruac Rites : Rain (Lvl3), Coils of Apep (Lvl4)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T13:56:21-07:00","id":568343,"title":"Cruac Rites : Rain (Lvl3), Coils of Apep (Lvl4)","content":"What is the functional difference really here? Rain seems to have more mechanics to it than Coils of Apep does, and is a lesser level Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:24:31-07:00","id":568382,"title":"","content":"Rain only works with precipitation. You can bring about rain, fog, sleet, snow, or clear skies. But otherwise, it's going to be normal.. Thrashing of Apep's Coils can bring about more extreme weather, including lightning and wind and probably sandstorms in certain areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T15:40:55-07:00","id":568447,"title":"","content":"I can understand that, but there is no applicable mechanic of any kind listed for the higher level Rite that I can tell.<br /> <br /> So the higher level Rite can call up more kinds of things, but short of making things wet, icy, or dirty, there are no apparent mechanical benefits?<br /> <br /> Listed benefits, not the benefits a ST might drum up for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:01:15-07:00","id":568464,"title":"","content":"I mean, if what you're asking for is the listed benefits, they're right there in the book. No one here is going to be able to tell you more about that than the book itself does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T16:29:38-07:00","id":568479,"title":"","content":"The core book has many suggestions for modifiers due to bad or extreme weather in the Attributes and Skills sections. There's probably some other suggestions elsewhere, in second edition you use environmental tilts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[